<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength — MorphoEval overall 89.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 score 89.4, superseding Pass 1 (86.8). The three Pass 1 gaps are closed in the model rather than in the scores. segment_specimen now closes the spine fringe and labels three tests (circularity 0.730, 0.725, 0.730; aspects 1.035, 0.998, 0.949). Ocellus peaks use a one-period window (71 peaks); their spacing sample has mean 49.21 µm, CV 0.330, and KS 0.415 against a normal centred on the FFT wavelength 60.336 µm. The comparison figure marks the equal-diffusion bar \"ablated\" and the 10 µm bar \"quenched\". The wavelength law is unchanged: Pearson r = 0.9965, RMSE = 2.575 µm, GIF 560 px × 12 frames, CV similarity 85.2 against USNM E39365. What remains is structural: nearest neighbours are shorter and more variable than the Fourier period, and the diffusivities are calibrations. Overall 89.4/100 (faithfulness 89.4, reproducibility 89.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 968c2bf7; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 87, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: docs/media/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 968c2bf7, image/png, 422557 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 584686888a3f82ed05a18420f2fac65b10ad03187e47388b8ca6ad1bb633a4c5 (sha256 584686888a3f82ed05a18420f2fac65b10ad03187e47388b8ca6ad1bb633a4c5), spec_fingerprint e8201a3df779a67d8e85472abacbae9a6fbc7d0d99dd6ba261bbc538d065da4c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e8201a3df779a67d8e85472abacbae9a6fbc7d0d99dd6ba261bbc538d065da4c; artifact_sha256: 584686888a3f82ed05a18420f2fac65b10ad03187e47388b8ca6ad1bb633a4c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=35136a28b3d11ab4..., datasets/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0/echinarachnius_parma_usnm_e39365_specimen.jpeg=1af65dc69de55d4b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v | Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) short-range activation with long-range inhibition; Kondo and Miura (2010) reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework | Seilacher (1979) constructional morphology of the sand-dollar test at centimetre scale; reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Fourier IMEX Schnakenberg integration on a 480 µm patch. Equilibrated FFT wavelength 60.336 µm; linear peak 61.343 µm; Pearson r 0.9965 across seven diffusivity scales; RMSE 2.575 µm | Equal-diffusion ablation amplitude 5.69e-3, marked on the figure. 10 µm predecessor patch amplitude 0, marked quenched | USNM E39365 split into 3 discs after a 15 px closing: mean circularity 0.730 versus union circularity 0.066; mean aspect 0.994 versus union aspect 1.413 | 71 ocellus peaks picked with a one-period window. Mean spacing 49.21 µm, CV 0.330, KS 0.415 against Normal(λ_FFT, s); transfer_boundary: Du and Dv place the lattice on the assigned 60 µm scale. They are not measured sand-dollar diffusivities. | Seilacher (1979) does not report a 60 µm pigment spacing. The chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma; the predecessor and successor are the 10 µm and 600 µm scale tiers. | Nearest-neighbour distance is not the FFT period. The radial spectrum carries the wavelength law; the spacing distribution is broader (CV 0.33).; does_not_claim: A measured echinochrome diffusion constant, a pigment gene network, or a fit to the centimetre-scale petaloid | That the 49 µm nearest-neighbour mean equals the 60 µm Turing wavelength | Sibling slot 160 parameters (α = 1.71, β = 0.43)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Nearest-neighbour spacing remains shorter and broader than the FFT period (mean 49.21 µm, CV 0.330, KS 0.415 versus Normal centred at 60.336 µm). The wavelength law is the radial spectrum, which already tracks the linear peak at r = 0.9965; a further lattice-phase fit is not required for the gates." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.94e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

